From 8b07b6daae85e16d49e5a0cc4828c459860589b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Jun 2026 14:47:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00669/11362] [outer-loop] Sudoku EBT: near-perfect SCORER,
 FAILED generator (decode is the wall)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EBT energy converged to a near-perfect Sudoku-validity SCORER (NCE loss 0.0001;
gold energy ~0 vs corrupted ~17, a 17-unit gap). But DECODING that energy fails
completely: per-cell argmin AND continuous energy-descent both give 0.000 exact-
grid solve-rate, blank-cell accuracy 0.109 (= 1/9 chance), and 132-145 mean
constraint violations — WORSE than random (AR baseline: 7.6). Mechanism:
contrastive training shapes the energy only near valid solutions (gold +/- local
corruption), so the global landscape the decoder searches from a blank grid is
full of bad minima the energy never learned. FUNDAMENTAL finding: a perfect energy
SCORER is not a GENERATOR; the wall is the decode/search + global landscape
shaping, not energy learning. Far more precise than P1's inconclusive arithmetic.
Refiner (the other generator paradigm) next.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
